WEBVTT

00:02.560 --> 00:05.530
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:05.630 --> 00:08.990
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:09.250 --> 00:10.790
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:11.630 --> 00:13.400
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:13.500 --> 00:17.230
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:17.340 --> 00:20.170
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:20.540 --> 00:22.170
They are also known as...

00:22.410 --> 00:24.850
the Shinigami.

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
nureta hitomi no oku

00:25.110 --> 00:31.780
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:33.490 --> 00:43.800
The pale moon quietly descends

00:33.570 --> 00:42.820
Yami no Matsuei

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
azayaka na sekai wa

00:50.110 --> 00:55.980
The splendid world

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:58.350 --> 01:08.420
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:08.520 --> 01:16.160
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:16.260 --> 01:22.790
A new era beckons now

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:25.510 --> 01:30.600
The injured black wings

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:30.780 --> 01:37.150
Shine in the moonlight

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
utsukushiku maiagare

01:37.750 --> 01:41.950
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:42.090 --> 01:47.290
The crimson kiss

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:47.400 --> 01:54.230
Flows deeply into the soul

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
soshite yume no naka e

01:54.400 --> 02:00.200
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:11.380 --> 02:12.250
Secret Room

02:23.720 --> 02:26.310
Count! Count!

02:26.620 --> 02:27.580
What?!

02:28.090 --> 02:31.450
I'm in heaven!

02:32.890 --> 02:35.360
It was worth getting up early to line up for it.

02:35.460 --> 02:38.190
Cakes again, huh?
You King of Sweet Tooths.

02:38.300 --> 02:40.160
I just love them!

02:40.260 --> 02:43.320
Dessert time is what I look forward to most.

02:43.430 --> 02:44.460
Whatever...

02:45.440 --> 02:47.630
So, time to dig in!

02:47.740 --> 02:49.070
Tsuzuki-san! Hisoka-san!

02:49.210 --> 02:51.230
Wh-What do you want, Gushoushin?

02:51.340 --> 02:52.600
I don't have any for you.

02:52.710 --> 02:55.040
Boss Konoe wants to see the both of you.

02:55.150 --> 02:57.410
He said for you to come right away.

02:57.520 --> 02:59.640
Oh, but--

03:00.750 --> 03:05.490
This next case is a request from
the Count at the Hall of Candles.

03:05.990 --> 03:07.460
- From the count?
- Yes.

03:08.190 --> 03:11.060
Some strange incidents
have been occurring lately.

03:11.160 --> 03:12.960
An unusual phenomena

03:13.060 --> 03:16.160
like people on the verge of death
suddenly gaining longevity.

03:16.270 --> 03:17.230
What do you mean?

03:17.340 --> 03:19.270
According to our investigation

03:19.370 --> 03:22.770
there were common traits
among each of the subjects.

03:22.870 --> 03:25.740
I'm sure you've heard of the Kakyouin Group?

03:25.840 --> 03:29.610
Is that the company which
has been booming lately?

03:29.710 --> 03:31.110
That's right.

03:31.220 --> 03:35.410
That company owns a luxury
liner called the Queen Camellia.

03:35.520 --> 03:38.320
All of the subjects had been
passengers on that ship.

03:38.420 --> 03:41.190
We can't just dismiss it as
some sort of coincidence.

03:41.290 --> 03:42.420
Here's what I want.

03:42.530 --> 03:44.620
You two are going to get aboard that ship

03:44.730 --> 03:47.490
and pin down the cause of those incidents.

03:48.070 --> 03:50.760
I'll have the Gushoushin twins
act as a conduit between us.

03:50.870 --> 03:52.170
- All right?
- Yes, sir.

03:52.700 --> 03:55.330
The ship is currently docked
at the port of Hakata.

03:55.440 --> 03:58.700
It will embark shortly,
so head out there right away.

03:58.810 --> 04:00.610
But I was about to eat my cake.

04:00.710 --> 04:03.270
Not to worry, Tsuzuki-san.

04:03.380 --> 04:06.320
We will be enjoying your cake for you.

04:06.420 --> 04:07.380
What?!

04:07.520 --> 04:09.780
- Have a problem with that?
- No.

04:09.890 --> 04:13.550
And also, don't you forget to bring us a souvenir.

04:13.660 --> 04:14.750
Yes, sir.

04:14.830 --> 04:19.880
Episode 7: The King of Swords, Part 1

04:42.620 --> 04:44.320
It looks like we got ourselves in quite nicely.

04:44.420 --> 04:45.390
Yeah.

04:45.490 --> 04:49.080
He's the head of the Kakyouin Group.
The owner of this ship.

04:49.630 --> 04:52.030
I have to keep an eye on him, right?

04:52.130 --> 04:54.650
That's right.
This is quite the case after all.

04:54.770 --> 04:57.860
I can't imagine the owner
not knowing anything.

04:58.200 --> 05:00.570
You must be Hibiki Azumi-kun.

05:00.670 --> 05:03.200
Yes. You've helped my father out a lot.

05:03.310 --> 05:04.970
Well, well. It goes both ways.

05:05.340 --> 05:08.940
This might be a rather boring
place for a young man like you.

05:09.050 --> 05:10.740
But I hope you enjoy yourself.

05:10.850 --> 05:11.820
Thank you very much.

05:12.020 --> 05:13.510
By the way, what's that?

05:13.620 --> 05:17.490
Oh. This is a new toy our company
is putting on the market.

05:17.860 --> 05:18.880
When you do this...

05:20.020 --> 05:20.990
Ow!

05:21.330 --> 05:23.490
That's what it does.

05:23.590 --> 05:25.690
My, my, that's quite the toy.

05:25.800 --> 05:27.730
Well, enjoy yourself.

05:29.800 --> 05:31.890
Good thing he didn't figure out you're a fake.

05:32.000 --> 05:35.910
Yeah. Hibiki Azumi's been living abroad so long

05:36.010 --> 05:38.340
nobody would recognize his face.

05:39.010 --> 05:42.970
<i>Here I'll be able to hear what
the passengers are saying.</i>

05:43.580 --> 05:46.310
<i>I hope I can get some clues on this case.</i>

05:46.750 --> 05:49.880
<i>So this is Wakabayashi Shozo, the politician.</i>

05:49.990 --> 05:52.620
<i>He's been in trouble within
his Taka faction lately</i>

05:52.720 --> 05:54.020
<i>for his excessive lifestyle.</i>

05:54.130 --> 05:57.360
<i>And this is Hojo Kanako, the actress.</i>

05:57.460 --> 05:59.790
<i>There's a rumor she's his lover.</i>

05:59.900 --> 06:02.560
Hey, can you get on with it?

06:02.670 --> 06:05.160
Haven't you heard that "time is money"?

06:05.270 --> 06:06.460
Uh, excuse me.

06:06.570 --> 06:09.160
May I see your cards, please?

06:09.470 --> 06:11.170
I have a straight.

06:11.280 --> 06:13.770
Ha. I lose.
I only have two pairs.

06:14.380 --> 06:16.310
Full house. Queens.

06:17.520 --> 06:20.540
The dealer wins, so that means a double tip.

06:21.820 --> 06:25.350
You're pretty good.
We just keep on losing.

06:25.460 --> 06:27.420
No. I'm just lucky. That's all.

06:27.890 --> 06:29.660
To hell with it. Let's go.

06:29.760 --> 06:31.590
Uh, wait. Sir!

06:32.700 --> 06:33.720
Ow...

06:33.830 --> 06:36.060
My, my. Are you all right?

06:36.170 --> 06:37.430
Uh, I'm fine!

06:37.540 --> 06:40.440
He didn't have to hit you with that ring of his.

06:40.540 --> 06:42.840
- Take care of it.
- Thank you.

06:43.940 --> 06:46.670
<i>This is the heir to the Abiko
Pharmaceuticals fortune.</i>

06:46.780 --> 06:49.110
<i>Abiko Tetsuhiro, a medical student.</i>

06:49.210 --> 06:50.940
<i>Right. I think I remember everyone.</i>

06:51.050 --> 06:52.070
Right.

06:52.180 --> 06:55.120
You're new here, so I'll tell you
a few things about this ship.

06:55.220 --> 06:57.350
I think it's best not to leave your cabin.

06:57.460 --> 06:59.150
This ship is kind of haunted.

06:59.260 --> 07:02.190
- Haunted?
- You know, like, by a ghost.

07:02.460 --> 07:03.430
What?!

07:03.530 --> 07:06.590
A woman ghost wanders
around here every night.

07:06.700 --> 07:09.760
Oh, but don't tell anyone I told you that.

07:11.900 --> 07:12.990
A ghost, huh?

07:21.580 --> 07:23.810
There doesn't seem to be
anything suspicious here.

07:23.910 --> 07:25.210
Yeah.

07:29.350 --> 07:31.080
You gave me a fright.

07:31.190 --> 07:32.210
I'm sorry.

07:34.160 --> 07:35.130
Thank you.

07:39.830 --> 07:42.230
Hey, would you like to dance with me?

08:12.000 --> 08:13.360
That was so much fun.

08:13.460 --> 08:16.430
I was getting so bored with
all the grown-ups on this ship.

08:16.530 --> 08:18.130
Hey, what's your name?

08:18.240 --> 08:19.530
Hibiki Azumi.

08:19.640 --> 08:24.200
Oh, Hibiki-san's son.
I'm Tsubaki. Kakyouin Tsubaki.

08:24.580 --> 08:26.270
Call me Princess Tsubaki.

08:26.380 --> 08:27.670
Princess Tsubaki?

08:34.790 --> 08:37.280
A good year for Chateau Margaux.

08:37.390 --> 08:39.950
A gift from the owner.

08:40.060 --> 08:41.290
Oh?

08:42.190 --> 08:44.750
Oh, dear.
I wonder what the fuss is?

08:49.930 --> 08:51.160
That man--

08:51.370 --> 08:54.670
I'm telling you there's
nothing suspicious about me.

08:54.770 --> 08:56.640
I just had some business with Hibiki-san.

09:01.910 --> 09:04.470
Speak to me in Japanese!

09:08.090 --> 09:09.580
Ow!

09:22.500 --> 09:25.440
You sure are slow, aren't you?

09:25.540 --> 09:27.970
I threw it expecting that you'd dodge it.

09:28.440 --> 09:32.270
It is because of that,
that I feel I can't but get involved.

09:34.650 --> 09:37.440
It's been a while, Tsuzuki-san.

09:37.980 --> 09:39.210
Muraki!

09:41.190 --> 09:42.810
Thank you for walking me back.

09:43.190 --> 09:44.780
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

09:44.890 --> 09:46.790
Just too much activity.
That's all.

09:47.890 --> 09:51.560
The doctor told me to take it easy,
but I got carried away.

09:51.660 --> 09:52.630
Doctor?

09:53.800 --> 09:58.390
Have some. A nice rose wine
that matches your eyes.

09:58.500 --> 10:00.130
So, you were still alive.

10:00.910 --> 10:03.900
You think I would've died
from something like that?

10:04.010 --> 10:05.600
How naive.

10:05.810 --> 10:09.010
Cut the crap.
What are you up to this time?

10:09.450 --> 10:11.140
How regrettable.

10:11.250 --> 10:14.740
Why do you always have to
think I'm plotting something?

10:15.350 --> 10:19.150
I do still carry out my practice
as a physician, you know.

10:19.260 --> 10:20.950
Yeah, right.

10:21.060 --> 10:25.390
I'll never forgive you for
what you did at Nagasaki.

10:27.000 --> 10:31.560
Are you suggesting that I'm
looking for my next sacrificial lamb?

10:31.670 --> 10:34.760
If that were the case, what would you do?

10:36.770 --> 10:40.040
As usual, you have your piercing eyes.

10:47.520 --> 10:51.350
Maybe I'm drawn to those eyes of yours.

11:04.170 --> 11:07.070
Hold it!
We're not finished talking yet!

11:07.170 --> 11:11.610
I am not on this ship because I'm after you.

11:11.710 --> 11:14.680
I'm the owner's daughter's doctor.

11:17.210 --> 11:19.550
Wh-What?!

11:21.150 --> 11:23.810
What? What did you just say?

11:24.090 --> 11:27.580
I was just saying that Dr. Muraki is my doctor

11:27.690 --> 11:30.020
and that he's such a wonderful person.

11:30.130 --> 11:33.030
Muraki!
Don't tell me he's on this ship?

11:34.730 --> 11:36.100
No!

11:37.100 --> 11:40.500
Oh, that must be the doctor.
It's open!

11:45.940 --> 11:50.440
Well. So you're on this ship too.
What a coincidence.

11:50.950 --> 11:52.510
Muraki...

11:57.690 --> 12:00.450
Boy, oh, boy.
I finally got away.

12:00.690 --> 12:03.560
That Hisoka gets pretty
mad when I make him wait.

12:03.660 --> 12:06.630
Now, come on, Wakabayashi.

12:07.630 --> 12:09.660
There's no reason why you can't do it.

12:09.770 --> 12:11.500
This is your ship after all.

12:11.600 --> 12:12.570
Nevertheless...

12:12.670 --> 12:17.300
I know what you've been
doing on this ship.

12:17.410 --> 12:20.240
I don't think you'd want people to know.

12:21.280 --> 12:25.940
Kakyouin. I haven't come into much luck today.

12:26.050 --> 12:29.710
I'm sure you know what the next game will be.

12:35.690 --> 12:38.720
I didn't know you knew Azumi, Doctor.

12:38.830 --> 12:41.350
I do know people despite what you think.

12:41.470 --> 12:44.800
Here's your medicine for today.
Take it.

12:52.340 --> 12:53.640
Good girl.

12:58.820 --> 13:01.380
Good night, Princess Tsubaki.

13:10.960 --> 13:12.390
What happened?!

13:30.890 --> 13:35.390
Yami no Matsuei

13:44.160 --> 13:46.630
I have the results of the autopsy.

13:48.970 --> 13:51.530
Based on the onset of rigor mortis

13:51.640 --> 13:55.470
Wakabayashi-san's time of death is estimated
at between 3 and 4 in the morning.

13:55.910 --> 13:58.810
The cause of death is
asphyxiation due to poisoning.

13:58.910 --> 14:01.100
It appears that Wakabayashi-san's heart

14:01.210 --> 14:03.980
was ripped out of his body after his death.

14:04.080 --> 14:06.170
Then... was Wakabayashi-sama--

14:06.280 --> 14:09.080
Yes. He was murdered.

14:09.190 --> 14:11.250
- By someone amongst us.
- What?!

14:11.360 --> 14:13.480
Hey, what do you mean by that?

14:13.590 --> 14:18.390
This deck is restricted to VIPs and,
as such, the security is thorough.

14:18.500 --> 14:21.760
I can't imagine someone from
the common classes did it. Right?

14:21.870 --> 14:23.200
Good point.

14:23.300 --> 14:24.730
But who on earth could have--

14:24.840 --> 14:27.460
The culprit is the owner.

14:28.210 --> 14:31.970
I knew very well that you wanted
to break ties with Wakabayashi.

14:32.080 --> 14:35.370
What?! My father wouldn't do such a thing!

14:35.480 --> 14:37.310
Why would I commit a murder

14:37.410 --> 14:39.810
knowing full well I'd be the first to be accused?

14:39.920 --> 14:41.380
Well, I wonder?

14:41.490 --> 14:44.150
That could've been part of your plan.

14:44.250 --> 14:48.280
Maybe it was the ghost that did it.

14:49.190 --> 14:50.990
I mean, I heard it last night.

14:51.090 --> 14:54.690
Strange footsteps in the
hallway late last night.

14:59.540 --> 15:00.940
Who is that?!

15:01.040 --> 15:05.480
I bet that that female ghost was
going off to kill Wakabayashi-san.

15:05.580 --> 15:07.040
That's ridiculous.

15:07.140 --> 15:10.050
A medical student like you believes in ghosts?

15:10.150 --> 15:12.710
A human did the murder.
Not a ghost.

15:12.820 --> 15:15.610
The envelope is blank.

15:19.220 --> 15:21.380
"To my love, Princess Tsubaki."

15:21.960 --> 15:25.420
"I am one who truly loves you."

15:25.530 --> 15:29.470
"I place the sacrificial heart upon the altar."

15:29.570 --> 15:31.530
"It is the Ace of Wands"?

15:31.640 --> 15:33.660
A message from the murderer?

15:33.770 --> 15:35.430
Know anything about that?

15:35.540 --> 15:39.740
No. Why is it addressed to me?
It's giving me the creeps.

15:40.410 --> 15:41.380
What's this?

15:41.480 --> 15:42.470
"The beginning."

15:43.110 --> 15:46.280
That's the Ace of Wands?
A tarot card?

15:46.380 --> 15:48.580
It's the first card.
So it means the beginning.

15:48.690 --> 15:50.350
The beginning?!

15:50.450 --> 15:54.720
You've got to be kidding!
Is someone else going to be murdered?!

15:56.360 --> 15:59.730
Regardless, we can never be too careful.

16:00.400 --> 16:03.370
We don't know who the murderer is after all.

16:10.740 --> 16:12.470
What do you think, Hisoka?

16:12.580 --> 16:16.310
I can't help but think Muraki's involved in this.

16:16.410 --> 16:19.640
I can't think of anyone else who could be guilty.

16:19.750 --> 16:21.080
Yeah.

16:23.490 --> 16:25.110
Good evening, Tsuzuki-san.

16:25.220 --> 16:26.450
Muraki.

16:27.060 --> 16:30.190
I really wanted to see you.

16:30.690 --> 16:34.630
They're for you.
Roses I picked out especially for you.

16:34.730 --> 16:38.030
Red queens.
Suits you very nicely.

16:38.770 --> 16:40.070
What are you trying to pull?

16:40.170 --> 16:44.130
Oh, my. I suggest that you
don't get on my wrong side.

16:44.240 --> 16:46.800
I don't think you want
your identity revealed here.

16:48.180 --> 16:52.710
Tsuzuki-san, how about a game of poker?

16:52.820 --> 16:55.650
No chips.
We'll wager with something else.

16:55.750 --> 16:56.980
Something else?

16:57.420 --> 17:00.220
Yes. For example, your body.

17:02.130 --> 17:04.220
What are you thinking?!

17:04.330 --> 17:06.320
A game. A game.

17:06.430 --> 17:09.890
Are you afraid that you will lose against me?

17:10.000 --> 17:11.660
Then what happens if I win?

17:11.770 --> 17:12.930
Let's see...

17:13.040 --> 17:15.630
In the off chance that you win

17:15.740 --> 17:18.670
I'll give you the information I have.

17:19.140 --> 17:23.010
It has to do with the woman ghost.
Interested?

17:26.750 --> 17:27.880
Are you serious?!

17:27.990 --> 17:30.480
My hand is a full house. Kings.

17:30.590 --> 17:33.520
Your hand is a hearts flush.
Well, it's over.

17:33.620 --> 17:36.460
"It can't be!"

17:38.700 --> 17:40.860
So, Tsuzuki-san.

17:41.400 --> 17:44.230
You will be mine for this one night.

17:54.780 --> 17:56.580
Hold it.

17:59.720 --> 18:01.950
How about a hand of poker, Doctor?

18:02.050 --> 18:04.650
If I win, you let the dealer off?

18:04.760 --> 18:07.190
You're going to try to save me?

18:07.560 --> 18:09.860
Sure. I'll accept.

18:10.360 --> 18:14.350
The more I'm teased now,
the more pleasure later.

18:15.090 --> 18:17.010
Prize

18:21.140 --> 18:22.830
Please place your bets.

18:22.940 --> 18:24.030
I'll put in ten.

18:26.880 --> 18:27.870
I'll raise you.

18:29.380 --> 18:31.680
You suspect me, don't you?

18:32.080 --> 18:33.050
I call.

18:33.150 --> 18:35.980
However, I have an alibi.

18:36.090 --> 18:38.820
If you have any suspicions,
go talk to Princess Tsubaki.

18:40.920 --> 18:46.330
Then again, maybe the better the alibi,
the more suspicions it raises.

18:46.430 --> 18:49.330
Moreover, I'm the one who did
the autopsy on Wakabayashi-san.

18:49.430 --> 18:51.330
What do you mean by that?

18:51.440 --> 18:55.500
I just had to give a fake time of
death and that solves it for me.

18:55.610 --> 18:57.040
No?

19:03.280 --> 19:04.680
You really did it.

19:04.780 --> 19:07.010
- Your hand?
- Sure.

19:07.120 --> 19:08.740
Show your hand, please.

19:08.850 --> 19:10.110
Four twos.

19:10.220 --> 19:13.050
This should settle it, Doctor.

19:16.760 --> 19:20.030
Incredible!
A royal straight flush!

19:21.060 --> 19:22.400
All right.

19:22.730 --> 19:24.330
I'll withdraw this time.

19:25.670 --> 19:26.970
Th-Thank god!

19:27.500 --> 19:29.270
H-Hold it, Muraki!

19:29.370 --> 19:31.600
You promised to give me information.

19:32.710 --> 19:37.370
There was a woman called Eileen
who was a passenger on this ship.

19:37.480 --> 19:42.890
But then she suddenly
went missing from the ship.

19:42.990 --> 19:46.920
Ever since, unusual things have
happened on this ship at night.

19:47.020 --> 19:48.510
Don't play dumb with me.

19:48.630 --> 19:51.030
Perhaps you were involved in that one too.

19:51.730 --> 19:55.600
You're going to refuse to believe
anything I say, aren't you?

19:57.730 --> 20:01.500
I hope you'll believe me when I die myself.

20:17.350 --> 20:18.620
Who's that?

20:19.920 --> 20:23.550
Um, Dr. Muraki hasn't come to
see me for my regular check-up.

20:23.660 --> 20:27.820
I went to his cabin, but it was locked.
And there was no answer.

20:27.930 --> 20:29.130
It couldn't be...!

20:34.170 --> 20:36.040
Open up!
You're there, aren't you!?

20:36.140 --> 20:38.400
Doctor! Doctor!

20:40.880 --> 20:42.470
Steward, I need the key!

20:42.580 --> 20:43.550
Yes, sir.

21:01.000 --> 21:02.160
Doctor?

21:19.980 --> 21:20.970
Muraki...

21:21.590 --> 21:24.520
No... This can't be! Doctor!

21:25.160 --> 21:27.020
<i>What on earth is going on?!</i>

21:27.120 --> 21:28.950
<i>How could Muraki have been killed?!</i>

21:40.420 --> 21:43.420
Next Episode

21:43.440 --> 21:46.500
The serial murders and
the signs of the tarot cards.

21:47.040 --> 21:49.070
Muraki has become one of the victims.

21:49.280 --> 21:51.800
Muraki died?!
How can that be?!

21:52.420 --> 21:55.650
The tarot cards of death
result in another sacrifice.

21:55.750 --> 21:58.450
Then who's the new suspect?

22:00.460 --> 22:04.990
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The King of Swords, Part 2

22:00.610 --> 22:10.490
Episode 8     The King of Swords, Part 2

22:05.400 --> 22:08.890
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:18.330 --> 22:21.690
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:18.330 --> 22:21.690
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.800 --> 22:24.730
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.800 --> 22:24.730
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.830 --> 22:28.320
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.830 --> 22:28.320
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:28.440 --> 22:31.030
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:28.440 --> 22:31.030
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:31.140 --> 22:38.370
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:31.140 --> 22:38.370
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:38.480 --> 22:45.110
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:38.480 --> 22:45.110
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:58.570 --> 23:04.990
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:58.570 --> 23:04.990
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:05.510 --> 23:11.440
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:05.510 --> 23:11.440
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:12.210 --> 23:18.550
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:12.210 --> 23:18.550
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:19.300 --> 23:24.700
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:19.300 --> 23:24.700
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
